{"absolutePath":"/home/claude/razum-dc/hermes-desktop/lat.md/desktop-updates.md","content":"# Desktop Updates\n\nDesktop updates use GitHub releases and expose both a startup upgrade action and a Settings auto-upgrade preference.\n\nThe Electron main process configures `electron-updater` against the repository publisher metadata from `electron-builder.yml`, which points at `fathah/hermes-desktop`. [[src/main/app/updater.ts#setupUpdater]] registers update IPC handlers, persists the auto-upgrade preference under Electron `userData`, and applies that preference to `autoUpdater.autoDownload`.\n\nWhen GitHub reports a newer release, [[src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/Layout.tsx#Layout]] shows an upgrade button in the sidebar footer as soon as the app reaches the main layout. The button downloads the update when needed, shows download progress, and changes into a restart action after the update is ready.\n\n[[src/renderer/src/components/settings/AboutPane.tsx#AboutPane]] (the About & Updates pane of the settings modal) presents the desktop app as its own card, separate from the Hermes Agent engine card — the two update on independent channels. The card shows the app version, the auto-upgrade toggle, and an explicit update action: [[src/renderer/src/components/settings/useSettingsData.ts#useSettingsData]] subscribes to the same `onUpdateAvailable`/`onUpdateDownloadProgress`/`onUpdateDownloaded`/`onUpdateError` events as the footer button and adds a manual `checkDesktopUpdate` (via `checkForUpdates`) plus a `handleDesktopUpdate` that downloads, then restarts via `installUpdate`. When auto-upgrade is enabled the startup release check downloads automatically; when disabled, downloading waits for the user's click (footer button or this card's action).\n\n## Local Windows portable build\n\n`npm run build:portable` creates an unsigned portable executable on a standard Windows account without requiring Developer Mode or administrator rights.\n\nThe dedicated `electron-builder.portable.yml` profile disables executable resource editing and signing, avoiding the legacy `winCodeSign` archive and its privileged symlink extraction. The regular `build:win` release path remains unchanged.\n","path":"desktop-updates.md","projectPath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","frontmatter":{},"sections":[{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates","heading":"Desktop Updates","depth":1,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[{"id":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates#Local Windows portable build","heading":"Local Windows portable build","depth":2,"file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","filePath":"lat.md/desktop-updates.md","children":[],"startLine":11,"endLine":15,"firstParagraph":"`npm run build:portable` creates an unsigned portable executable on a standard Windows account without requiring Developer Mode or administrator rights.","githubSlug":"local-windows-portable-build"}],"startLine":1,"endLine":10,"firstParagraph":"Desktop updates use GitHub releases and expose both a startup upgrade action and a Settings auto-upgrade preference.","githubSlug":"desktop-updates"}],"headingTitles":["Desktop Updates","Local Windows portable build"],"wikiRefs":[{"target":"src/main/app/updater.ts#setupUpdater","fromSection":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates","file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","line":5},{"target":"src/renderer/src/screens/Layout/Layout.tsx#Layout","fromSection":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates","file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","line":7},{"target":"src/renderer/src/components/settings/AboutPane.tsx#AboutPane","fromSection":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates","file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","line":9},{"target":"src/renderer/src/components/settings/useSettingsData.ts#useSettingsData","fromSection":"lat.md/desktop-updates#Desktop Updates","file":"lat.md/desktop-updates","line":9}],"paragraphs":[{"markdown":"Desktop updates use GitHub releases and expose both a startup upgrade action and a Settings auto-upgrade pre